Description: Fits single, multi-class oblique classification trees in which
    each internal node's split is defined by a support vector machine
    hyperplane rather than a threshold on a single variable. Multi-class 
    problems are handled directly at every node with a one-vs-rest strategy i.e.,
    each class is tried in turn and the hyperplane that minimizes an
    impurity measure ('entropy' or Gini) is kept as the split. The approach
    follows the 'STree' algorithm of Montanana, Gamez and Puerta (2021)
    <doi:10.1007/978-3-030-85713-4_6>.
